#
# Counter-example for math:ArgumentSlotShape (derived from the min-1 qualified
# restrictions on math:ArgumentSlot's math:slotIndex and math:slotExpression): a
# math:ArgumentSlot naming its index but no expression. The narrowed
# math:MalformedArgumentSlot covers exactly this "not exactly one index and one
# expression" shape — duplicate-index slots are the separate math:DuplicateArgumentSlotIndex
# gate. Validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent
# (math:MalformedArgumentSlot).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:bareSlot a math:ArgumentSlot ;
    math:slotIndex 0 .
